>> title: Nước Chấm
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: fish sauce, lime, vietnamese, dipping sauce, no-cook
>> counters: Phở & Bánh Mì, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: nuoc cham, nước chấm, nuoc mam pha, nước mắm pha, fish sauce dressing, Vietnamese dipping sauce, dipping sauce, spring roll sauce, the sauce for spring rolls, table sauce
>> pairs-with: cha-gio, goi-cuon, bun-thit-nuong
>> servings: 8
>> time: 15 min

>> step: dissolve the sugar
Stir @granulated sugar{1/3%cup}(70 g) into @warm water{1%cup}(240 mL) until it disappears.

>> step: pound to a rough paste
Pound @garlic{3%cloves} and @Thai chiles{2}(stemmed) to a rough paste in a #mortar{}.

>> step: stir in the sauce and the lime
Stir @&(~2)sweetened water{} together with @fish sauce{1/3%cup}(80 mL) and @lime juice{1/3%cup}(80 mL; about 3 limes), and taste before you go further.

>> step: stir in the chile, stand 10 min
Stir @&(~2)garlic and chile{} into @&(~1)dressing{} with @shredded carrot{2%Tbs}, then ~stand{10%min} so the chile floats and the garlic stops tasting raw.
